{"route":"/docs/6.0/content/typography/","version":"6.0","renderedVersion":"6.0","title":{"id":"content","type":"heading","en":"Typography","level":1},"lead":{"id":"content--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Documentation and examples for Bootstrap typography, including global settings, headings, body text, lists, and more."},"blocks":[{"id":"global-settings","type":"heading","en":"Global settings","level":2},{"id":"global-settings--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Bootstrap sets basic global display, typography, and link styles. When more control is needed, check out our text utilities."},{"id":"global-settings--list-1","type":"list","tag":"ul","items":[{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"global-settings--item-1","type":"item","en":"Use a <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/content/reboot#native-font-stack\">native font stack</a> that selects the best <code>font-family</code> for each OS and device."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"global-settings--item-2","type":"item","en":"For a more inclusive and accessible type scale, we use the browser’s default root <code>font-size</code> (typically 16px) so visitors can customize their browser defaults as needed."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"global-settings--item-3","type":"item","en":"Use the <code>--body-font-family</code>, <code>--body-font-size</code>, and <code>--body-line-height</code> attributes as our typographic base applied to the <code>&lt;body&gt;</code>."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"global-settings--item-4","type":"item","en":"Set the global link color via <code>--bs-link-color</code>."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"global-settings--item-5","type":"item","en":"Use <code>--bs-body-bg</code> to set a <code>background-color</code> on the <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> (<code>#fff</code> by default)."}]}]},{"id":"global-settings--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"These styles can be found within <code>_reboot.scss</code>, and the global variables are defined in <code>_config.scss</code>. Make sure to set <code>--body-font-size</code> in <code>rem</code>."},{"id":"headings","type":"heading","en":"Headings","level":2},{"id":"headings--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"As mentioned in <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/content/reboot#headings\">Reboot</a>, all HTML headings, <code>&lt;h1&gt;</code> through <code>&lt;h6&gt;</code>, are available, as element or class selectors."},{"id":"headings--table-1","type":"table","caption":[],"rows":[{"head":true,"cells":[{"type":"th","body":[{"id":"headings--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Heading"}]},{"type":"th","body":[{"id":"headings--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"Example"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"headings--paragraph-4","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>&lt;h1&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"headings--paragraph-5","type":"paragraph","en":"h1. Bootstrap heading"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"headings--paragraph-6","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>&lt;h2&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"headings--paragraph-7","type":"paragraph","en":"h2. Bootstrap heading"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"headings--paragraph-8","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>&lt;h3&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"headings--paragraph-9","type":"paragraph","en":"h3. Bootstrap heading"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"headings--paragraph-10","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>&lt;h4&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"headings--paragraph-11","type":"paragraph","en":"h4. Bootstrap heading"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"headings--paragraph-12","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>&lt;h5&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"headings--paragraph-13","type":"paragraph","en":"h5. Bootstrap heading"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"headings--paragraph-14","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>&lt;h6&gt;&lt;/h6&gt;</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"headings--paragraph-15","type":"paragraph","en":"h6. Bootstrap heading"}]}]}]},{"id":"headings--code-1","type":"code","value":"<h1>h1. Bootstrap heading</h1>\n<h2>h2. Bootstrap heading</h2>\n<h3>h3. Bootstrap heading</h3>\n<h4>h4. Bootstrap heading</h4>\n<h5>h5. Bootstrap heading</h5>\n<h6>h6. Bootstrap heading</h6>\n\n<p class=\"h1\">h1. Bootstrap heading</p>\n<p class=\"h2\">h2. Bootstrap heading</p>\n<p class=\"h3\">h3. Bootstrap heading</p>\n<p class=\"h4\">h4. Bootstrap heading</p>\n<p class=\"h5\">h5. Bootstrap heading</p>\n<p class=\"h6\">h6. Bootstrap heading</p>","language":""},{"id":"headings--paragraph-16","type":"paragraph","en":"Head to our <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/utilities/font-size\">font size utilities</a> for more control over the <code>font-size</code> and <code>line-height</code>."},{"id":"global-font-sizes","type":"heading","en":"Global font sizes","level":2},{"id":"global-font-sizes--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Headings are sized with our responsive font-size root CSS variables. You can use these yourself, or with our heading classes, <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/utilities/font-size\">font size utilities</a>, and <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/utilities/font-size#with-line-height\">text size utilities</a> (where you’ll get a <code>line-height</code> as well)."},{"id":"global-font-sizes--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Learn more about how these work down below in the <a href=\"#css\">CSS</a> section."},{"id":"global-font-sizes--example-1","type":"demo","key":"8bacdf879d3e2ae05390","height":300},{"id":"global-font-sizes--code-1","type":"code","value":"<div class=\"fs-xs\">.fs-xs</div>\n<div class=\"fs-sm\">.fs-sm</div>\n<div class=\"fs-md\">.fs-md</div>\n<div class=\"fs-lg\">.fs-lg</div>\n<div class=\"fs-xl\">.fs-xl</div>\n<div class=\"fs-2xl\">.fs-2xl</div>\n<div class=\"fs-3xl\">.fs-3xl</div>\n<div class=\"fs-4xl\">.fs-4xl</div>\n<div class=\"fs-5xl\">.fs-5xl</div>\n<div class=\"fs-6xl\">.fs-6xl</div>","language":""},{"id":"inline-text-elements","type":"heading","en":"Inline text elements","level":2},{"id":"inline-text-elements--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Styling for common inline HTML5 elements."},{"id":"inline-text-elements--example-1","type":"demo","key":"c4d06647cfa1e007d3e5","height":300},{"id":"inline-text-elements--code-1","type":"code","value":"<p>You can use the mark tag to <mark>highlight</mark> text.</p>\n<p><del>This line of text is meant to be treated as deleted text.</del></p>\n<p><s>This line of text is meant to be treated as no longer accurate.</s></p>\n<p><ins>This line of text is meant to be treated as an addition to the document.</ins></p>\n<p><u>This line of text will render as underlined.</u></p>\n<p><small>This line of text is meant to be treated as fine print.</small></p>\n<p><strong>This line rendered as bold text.</strong></p>\n<p><em>This line rendered as italicized text.</em></p>","language":""},{"id":"inline-text-elements--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Beware that those tags should be used for semantic purpose:"},{"id":"inline-text-elements--list-1","type":"list","tag":"ul","items":[{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"inline-text-elements--item-1","type":"item","en":"<code>&lt;mark&gt;</code> represents text which is marked or highlighted for reference or notation purposes."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"inline-text-elements--item-2","type":"item","en":"<code>&lt;small&gt;</code> represents side-comments and small print, like copyright and legal text."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"inline-text-elements--item-3","type":"item","en":"<code>&lt;s&gt;</code> represents element that are no longer relevant or no longer accurate."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"inline-text-elements--item-4","type":"item","en":"<code>&lt;u&gt;</code> represents a span of inline text which should be rendered in a way that indicates that it has a non-textual annotation."}]}]},{"id":"inline-text-elements--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"If you want to style your text, you should use the following classes instead:"},{"id":"inline-text-elements--list-2","type":"list","tag":"ul","items":[{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"inline-text-elements--item-5","type":"item","en":"<code>.mark</code> will apply the same styles as <code>&lt;mark&gt;</code>."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"inline-text-elements--item-6","type":"item","en":"<code>.small</code> will apply the same styles as <code>&lt;small&gt;</code>."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"inline-text-elements--item-7","type":"item","en":"<code>.text-decoration-underline</code> will apply the same styles as <code>&lt;u&gt;</code>."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"inline-text-elements--item-8","type":"item","en":"<code>.text-decoration-line-through</code> will apply the same styles as <code>&lt;s&gt;</code>."}]}]},{"id":"inline-text-elements--paragraph-4","type":"paragraph","en":"While not shown above, feel free to use <code>&lt;b&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;i&gt;</code> in HTML5. <code>&lt;b&gt;</code> is meant to highlight words or phrases without conveying additional importance, while <code>&lt;i&gt;</code> is mostly for voice, technical terms, etc."},{"id":"text-utilities","type":"heading","en":"Text utilities","level":2},{"id":"text-utilities--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Utility classes are available for most common text-related CSS properties."},{"id":"text-utilities--list-1","type":"list","tag":"ul","items":[{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"text-utilities--item-1","type":"item","en":"<a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/utilities/font-family\">Font family</a>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"text-utilities--item-2","type":"item","en":"<a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/utilities/font-size\">Font size</a>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"text-utilities--item-3","type":"item","en":"<a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/utilities/font-style\">Font style</a>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"text-utilities--item-4","type":"item","en":"<a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/utilities/font-weight\">Font weight</a>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"text-utilities--item-5","type":"item","en":"<a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/utilities/line-height\">Line height</a>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"text-utilities--item-6","type":"item","en":"<a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/utilities/text-alignment\">Text alignment</a>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"text-utilities--item-7","type":"item","en":"<a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/utilities/text-transform\">Text transform</a>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"text-utilities--item-8","type":"item","en":"<a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/utilities/text-decoration\">Text decoration</a>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"text-utilities--item-9","type":"item","en":"<a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/utilities/text-wrapping\">Text wrapping</a>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"text-utilities--item-10","type":"item","en":"<a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/utilities/vertical-align\">Vertical alignment</a>"}]}]},{"id":"text-utilities--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Change text alignment, transform, style, weight, line-height, decoration and color with our text and <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/utilities/colors\">color utilities</a>."},{"id":"abbreviations","type":"heading","en":"Abbreviations","level":2},{"id":"abbreviations--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Stylized implementation of HTML’s <code>&lt;abbr&gt;</code> element for abbreviations and acronyms to show the expanded version on hover. Abbreviations have a default underline and gain a help cursor to provide additional context on hover and to users of assistive technologies."},{"id":"abbreviations--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Add <code>.initialism</code> to an abbreviation for a slightly smaller font-size."},{"id":"abbreviations--example-1","type":"demo","key":"a8840e08c127612b5ecd","height":174},{"id":"abbreviations--code-1","type":"code","value":"<p><abbr title=\"attribute\">attr</abbr></p>\n<p><abbr title=\"HyperText Markup Language\" class=\"initialism\">HTML</abbr></p>","language":""},{"id":"blockquotes","type":"heading","en":"Blockquotes","level":2},{"id":"blockquotes--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Wrap <code>&lt;blockquote class=&quot;blockquote&quot;&gt;</code> around any HTML to quote blocks of content from another source within your document. We make <code>.blockquote</code> a flex container for easier spacing, which means you can use <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/utilities/flex\">flex utilities</a> for alignment, spacing, and more."},{"id":"blockquotes--example-1","type":"demo","key":"edee5b35b7125e12cff7","height":147},{"id":"blockquotes--code-1","type":"code","value":"<blockquote class=\"blockquote\">\n  <p>A well-known quote, contained in a blockquote element.</p>\n</blockquote>","language":""},{"id":"blockquotes--example-2","type":"demo","key":"6ab0e2759fc0bac7ecf1","height":147},{"id":"blockquotes--code-2","type":"code","value":"<blockquote class=\"blockquote\">\n  <p>A well-known quote, contained in a blockquote element.</p>\n  <p>And the second part of the original quote—like another paragraph—would be placed here as well. This paragraph is a little longer to show how text would wrap within the blockquote styling.</p>\n</blockquote>","language":""},{"id":"sources","type":"heading","en":"Sources","level":3},{"id":"sources--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"The HTML spec requires that blockquote attribution be placed <strong>outside</strong> the <code>&lt;blockquote&gt;</code>. In this case, use a <code>&lt;figure&gt;</code> element and place the <code>.blockquote</code> class on it instead of the <code>&lt;blockquote&gt;</code> element. This ensures access to CSS variables across blockquote and attribution element."},{"id":"sources--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"For source attribution, use a <code>&lt;figcaption&gt;</code> or a block level element (e.g., <code>&lt;p&gt;</code>) with the <code>.blockquote-footer</code> class. Wrap the name of any source work in <code>&lt;cite&gt;</code> as well."},{"id":"sources--example-1","type":"demo","key":"2343a1b1809ac956ebd5","height":147},{"id":"sources--code-1","type":"code","value":"<figure class=\"blockquote\">\n  <blockquote>\n    <p>A well-known quote, contained in a blockquote element.</p>\n  </blockquote>\n  <figcaption class=\"blockquote-footer\">\n    Someone famous in <cite title=\"Source Title\">Source Title</cite>\n  </figcaption>\n</figure>","language":""},{"id":"nested","type":"heading","en":"Nested","level":3},{"id":"nested--example-1","type":"demo","key":"566e42d96c0d2cfc278a","height":147},{"id":"nested--code-1","type":"code","value":"<blockquote class=\"blockquote\">\n  <p>A well-known quote, contained in a blockquote element.</p>\n  <blockquote class=\"blockquote\">\n    <p>A well-known quote, contained in a blockquote element.</p>\n  </blockquote>\n</blockquote>","language":""},{"id":"alignment","type":"heading","en":"Alignment","level":3},{"id":"alignment--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Use text or flex utilities as needed to change the alignment of your blockquote."},{"id":"alignment--example-1","type":"demo","key":"99eb7519eca0da8a6388","height":147},{"id":"alignment--code-1","type":"code","value":"<figure class=\"blockquote text-center\">\n  <blockquote>\n    <p>A well-known quote, contained in a blockquote element.</p>\n  </blockquote>\n  <figcaption class=\"blockquote-footer\">\n    Someone famous in <cite title=\"Source Title\">Source Title</cite>\n  </figcaption>\n</figure>","language":""},{"id":"alignment--example-2","type":"demo","key":"f47e615c48b48051a311","height":147},{"id":"alignment--code-2","type":"code","value":"<figure class=\"blockquote align-items-end\">\n  <blockquote>\n    <p>A well-known quote, contained in a blockquote element.</p>\n  </blockquote>\n  <figcaption class=\"blockquote-footer\">\n    Someone famous in <cite title=\"Source Title\">Source Title</cite>\n  </figcaption>\n</figure>","language":""},{"id":"lists","type":"heading","en":"Lists","level":2},{"id":"unstyled","type":"heading","en":"Unstyled","level":3},{"id":"unstyled--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Remove the default <code>list-style</code> and left margin on list items (immediate children only). <strong>This only applies to immediate children list items</strong>, meaning you will need to add the class for any nested lists as well."},{"id":"unstyled--example-1","type":"demo","key":"45d94dc9dfd3c99548e4","height":147},{"id":"unstyled--code-1","type":"code","value":"<ul class=\"list-unstyled\">\n  <li>This is a list.</li>\n  <li>It appears completely unstyled.</li>\n  <li>Structurally, it’s still a list.</li>\n  <li>However, this style only applies to immediate child elements.</li>\n  <li>Nested lists:\n    <ul>\n      <li>are unaffected by this style</li>\n      <li>will still show a bullet</li>\n      <li>and have appropriate left margin</li>\n    </ul>\n  </li>\n  <li>This may still come in handy in some situations.</li>\n</ul>","language":""},{"id":"inline","type":"heading","en":"Inline","level":3},{"id":"inline--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Remove a list’s bullets and apply some light <code>margin</code> with a combination of two classes, <code>.list-inline</code> and <code>.list-inline-item</code>."},{"id":"inline--example-1","type":"demo","key":"8572a3add9739fcbd96f","height":147},{"id":"inline--code-1","type":"code","value":"<ul class=\"list-inline\">\n  <li class=\"list-inline-item\">This is a list item.</li>\n  <li class=\"list-inline-item\">And another one.</li>\n  <li class=\"list-inline-item\">But they’re displayed inline.</li>\n</ul>","language":""},{"id":"description-list-alignment","type":"heading","en":"Description list alignment","level":3},{"id":"description-list-alignment--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Align terms and descriptions horizontally by using our grid system’s predefined classes (or semantic mixins). For longer terms, you can optionally add a <code>.text-truncate</code> class to truncate the text with an ellipsis."},{"id":"description-list-alignment--example-1","type":"demo","key":"924d96c6fd7de018e854","height":147},{"id":"description-list-alignment--code-1","type":"code","value":"<dl class=\"row\">\n  <dt class=\"sm:col-3\">Description lists</dt>\n  <dd class=\"sm:col-9\">A description list is perfect for defining terms.</dd>\n\n  <dt class=\"sm:col-3\">Term</dt>\n  <dd class=\"sm:col-9\">\n    <p>Definition for the term.</p>\n    <p>And some more placeholder definition text.</p>\n  </dd>\n\n  <dt class=\"sm:col-3\">Another term</dt>\n  <dd class=\"sm:col-9\">This definition is short, so no extra paragraphs or anything.</dd>\n\n  <dt class=\"sm:col-3 text-truncate\">Truncated term is truncated</dt>\n  <dd class=\"sm:col-9\">This can be useful when space is tight. Adds an ellipsis at the end.</dd>\n\n  <dt class=\"sm:col-3\">Nesting</dt>\n  <dd class=\"sm:col-9\">\n    <dl class=\"row\">\n      <dt class=\"sm:col-4\">Nested definition list</dt>\n      <dd class=\"sm:col-8\">I heard you like definition lists. Let me put a definition list inside your definition list.</dd>\n    </dl>\n  </dd>\n</dl>","language":""},{"id":"responsive-font-sizes","type":"heading","en":"Responsive font sizes","level":2},{"id":"responsive-font-sizes--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Bootstrap uses CSS’s <code>clamp()</code> function to enable responsive font sizes, allowing text to scale more naturally across device and viewport sizes."},{"id":"css","type":"heading","en":"CSS","level":2},{"id":"variables","type":"heading","en":"Variables","level":3},{"id":"variables--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"All <code>--font-size-*</code> and <code>--line-height-*</code> CSS custom properties are defined in <code>_root.scss</code>, generated from the <code>$font-sizes</code> Sass map in <code>_config.scss</code>."},{"id":"variables--code-1","type":"code","value":":root {\n  /* Abbreviated list for example purposes… */\n  --font-size-xs: 0.75rem;\n  --font-size-sm: 0.875rem;\n  --font-size-md: 1rem;\n  --font-size-lg: 1.25rem;\n  --font-size-xl: 1.5rem;\n  /* Plus the rest… */\n}","language":""},{"id":"variables--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Headings, paragraphs, description lists, and <code>&lt;legend&gt;</code> elements—covered here and in <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/content/reboot\">Reboot</a>—use dedicated CSS variables for real-time customization, defined in <code>_reboot.scss</code>."},{"id":"variables--code-2","type":"code","value":"// stylelint-disable-next-line scss/dollar-variable-default\n$type-tokens: defaults(\n  (\n    --heading-margin-bottom: var(--spacer-2),\n    --heading-font-family: null,\n    --heading-font-style: null,\n    --heading-line-height: 1.2,\n    --paragraph-margin-bottom: var(--spacer),\n    --legend-margin-bottom: var(--spacer-2),\n    --legend-font-size: 1.5rem,\n    --legend-font-weight: null,\n    --list-padding-x: var(--spacer-7),\n  ),\n  $type-tokens\n);","language":""},{"id":"sass-maps","type":"heading","en":"Sass maps","level":3},{"id":"sass-maps--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"The <code>$font-sizes</code> map in <code>_config.scss</code> defines Bootstrap’s type scale. Each key (e.g., <code>xs</code>, <code>md</code>, <code>3xl</code>) holds a nested map with <code>font-size</code> and <code>line-height</code> values. Larger sizes use <code>clamp()</code> for responsive scaling."},{"id":"sass-maps--code-1","type":"code","value":"$font-sizes: ();\n// stylelint-disable-next-line scss/dollar-variable-default\n$font-sizes: defaults(\n  (\n    \"xs\": (\n      \"font-size\": .75rem,\n      \"line-height\": 1.25\n    ),\n    \"sm\": (\n      \"font-size\": .875rem,\n      \"line-height\": 1.5\n    ),\n    \"md\": (\n      \"font-size\": 1rem,\n      \"line-height\": 1.5\n    ),\n    \"lg\": (\n      \"font-size\": clamp(1.125rem, 1rem + .625vw, 1.25rem),\n      \"line-height\": 1.5\n    ),\n    \"xl\": (\n      \"font-size\": clamp(1.5rem, 1.1rem + .75vw, 1.75rem),\n      \"line-height\": calc(2.5 / 1.75)\n    ),\n    \"2xl\": (\n      \"font-size\": clamp(1.75rem, 1.3rem + 1vw, 2rem),\n      \"line-height\": calc(3 / 2.25)\n    ),\n    \"3xl\": (\n      \"font-size\": clamp(2rem, 1.5rem + 1.875vw, 2.5rem),\n      \"line-height\": 1.2\n    ),\n    \"4xl\": (\n      \"font-size\": clamp(2.25rem, 1.75rem + 2.5vw, 3rem),\n      \"line-height\": 1.1\n    ),\n    \"5xl\": (\n      \"font-size\": clamp(3rem, 2rem + 5vw, 4rem),\n      \"line-height\": 1.1\n    ),\n    \"6xl\": (\n      \"font-size\": clamp(3.75rem, 2.5rem + 6.25vw, 5rem),\n      \"line-height\": 1\n    ),\n  ),\n  $font-sizes\n);","language":""},{"id":"sass-maps--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"You can override individual keys, replace the entire map, or remove keys by setting them to <code>null</code>:"},{"id":"sass-maps--code-2","type":"code","value":"// Per-key override\n@use \"bootstrap/scss/config\" with (\n  $font-sizes: (\"xs\": (\"font-size\": .625rem, \"line-height\": 1.25))\n);\n\n// Remove a key\n@use \"bootstrap/scss/config\" with (\n  $font-sizes: (\"6xl\": null)\n);","language":""},{"id":"sass-loops","type":"heading","en":"Sass loops","level":3},{"id":"sass-loops--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"The font-size map is used to generate <code>--font-size-*</code> and <code>--line-height-*</code> CSS custom properties in <code>_root.scss</code>, as well as <code>.fs-*</code> and <code>.text-*</code> utility classes in <code>_utilities.scss</code>."},{"id":"sass-loops--code-1","type":"code","value":"// Generate font-size and line-height tokens\n@each $name, $props in $font-sizes {\n  $root-tokens: map.set($root-tokens, --font-size-#{$name}, map.get($props, \"font-size\"));\n  $root-tokens: map.set($root-tokens, --line-height-#{$name}, map.get($props, \"line-height\"));\n}","language":""},{"id":"sass-loops--code-2","type":"code","value":"\"font-size\": (\n  property: font-size,\n  class: fs,\n  values: map-get-nested($font-sizes, \"font-size\")\n),\n\"text-size\": (\n  property: (\n    \"font-size\": 1rem,\n    \"line-height\": 1.5\n  ),\n  class: text,\n  values: $font-sizes\n),","language":""}],"demos":[{"key":"8bacdf879d3e2ae05390","html":"<div class=\"fs-xs\">.fs-xs</div>\n<div class=\"fs-sm\">.fs-sm</div>\n<div class=\"fs-md\">.fs-md</div>\n<div class=\"fs-lg\">.fs-lg</div>\n<div class=\"fs-xl\">.fs-xl</div>\n<div class=\"fs-2xl\">.fs-2xl</div>\n<div class=\"fs-3xl\">.fs-3xl</div>\n<div class=\"fs-4xl\">.fs-4xl</div>\n<div class=\"fs-5xl\">.fs-5xl</div>\n<div class=\"fs-6xl\">.fs-6xl</div>","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""},{"key":"c4d06647cfa1e007d3e5","html":"<p>You can use the mark tag to <mark>highlight</mark> text.</p>\n<p><del>This line of text is meant to be treated as deleted text.</del></p>\n<p><s>This line of text is meant to be treated as no longer accurate.</s></p>\n<p><ins>This line of text is meant to be treated as an addition to the document.</ins></p>\n<p><u>This line of text will render as underlined.</u></p>\n<p><small>This line of text is meant to be treated as fine print.</small></p>\n<p><strong>This line rendered as bold text.</strong></p>\n<p><em>This line rendered as italicized text.</em></p>","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""},{"key":"a8840e08c127612b5ecd","html":"<p><abbr title=\"attribute\">attr</abbr></p>\n<p><abbr title=\"HyperText Markup Language\" class=\"initialism\">HTML</abbr></p>","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""},{"key":"edee5b35b7125e12cff7","html":"<blockquote class=\"blockquote\">\n  <p>A well-known quote, contained in a blockquote element.</p>\n</blockquote>","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""},{"key":"6ab0e2759fc0bac7ecf1","html":"<blockquote class=\"blockquote\">\n  <p>A well-known quote, contained in a blockquote element.</p>\n  <p>And the second part of the original quote—like another paragraph—would be placed here as well. This paragraph is a little longer to show how text would wrap within the blockquote styling.</p>\n</blockquote>","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""},{"key":"2343a1b1809ac956ebd5","html":"<figure class=\"blockquote\">\n  <blockquote>\n    <p>A well-known quote, contained in a blockquote element.</p>\n  </blockquote>\n  <figcaption class=\"blockquote-footer\">\n    Someone famous in <cite title=\"Source Title\">Source Title</cite>\n  </figcaption>\n</figure>","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""},{"key":"566e42d96c0d2cfc278a","html":"<blockquote class=\"blockquote\">\n  <p>A well-known quote, contained in a blockquote element.</p>\n  <blockquote class=\"blockquote\">\n    <p>A well-known quote, contained in a blockquote element.</p>\n  </blockquote>\n</blockquote>","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""},{"key":"99eb7519eca0da8a6388","html":"<figure class=\"blockquote text-center\">\n  <blockquote>\n    <p>A well-known quote, contained in a blockquote element.</p>\n  </blockquote>\n  <figcaption class=\"blockquote-footer\">\n    Someone famous in <cite title=\"Source Title\">Source Title</cite>\n  </figcaption>\n</figure>","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""},{"key":"f47e615c48b48051a311","html":"<figure class=\"blockquote align-items-end\">\n  <blockquote>\n    <p>A well-known quote, contained in a blockquote element.</p>\n  </blockquote>\n  <figcaption class=\"blockquote-footer\">\n    Someone famous in <cite title=\"Source Title\">Source Title</cite>\n  </figcaption>\n</figure>","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""},{"key":"45d94dc9dfd3c99548e4","html":"<ul class=\"list-unstyled\">\n  <li>This is a list.</li>\n  <li>It appears completely unstyled.</li>\n  <li>Structurally, it’s still a list.</li>\n  <li>However, this style only applies to immediate child elements.</li>\n  <li>Nested lists:\n    <ul>\n      <li>are unaffected by this style</li>\n      <li>will still show a bullet</li>\n      <li>and have appropriate left margin</li>\n    </ul>\n  </li>\n  <li>This may still come in handy in some situations.</li>\n</ul>","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""},{"key":"8572a3add9739fcbd96f","html":"<ul class=\"list-inline\">\n  <li class=\"list-inline-item\">This is a list item.</li>\n  <li class=\"list-inline-item\">And another one.</li>\n  <li class=\"list-inline-item\">But they’re displayed inline.</li>\n</ul>","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""},{"key":"924d96c6fd7de018e854","html":"<dl class=\"row\">\n  <dt class=\"sm:col-3\">Description lists</dt>\n  <dd class=\"sm:col-9\">A description list is perfect for defining terms.</dd>\n\n  <dt class=\"sm:col-3\">Term</dt>\n  <dd class=\"sm:col-9\">\n    <p>Definition for the term.</p>\n    <p>And some more placeholder definition text.</p>\n  </dd>\n\n  <dt class=\"sm:col-3\">Another term</dt>\n  <dd class=\"sm:col-9\">This definition is short, so no extra paragraphs or anything.</dd>\n\n  <dt class=\"sm:col-3 text-truncate\">Truncated term is truncated</dt>\n  <dd class=\"sm:col-9\">This can be useful when space is tight. Adds an ellipsis at the end.</dd>\n\n  <dt class=\"sm:col-3\">Nesting</dt>\n  <dd class=\"sm:col-9\">\n    <dl class=\"row\">\n      <dt class=\"sm:col-4\">Nested definition list</dt>\n      <dd class=\"sm:col-8\">I heard you like definition lists. Let me put a definition list inside your definition list.</dd>\n    </dl>\n  </dd>\n</dl>","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""}],"nav":[{"en":"Install","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/install"},{"en":"AI","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/ai"},{"en":"Approach","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/approach"},{"en":"CSS variables","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/css-variables"},{"en":"JavaScript","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/javascript"},{"en":"Browsers & devices","href":"https://g